<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18060" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔχ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thing boasted of, object of pride, the pride, boast,</i>
				&lt;<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθονός</span>&gt; <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				710
			</span></i> (lyr.); <i>cause for boasting, glory,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ γάρ νιν εἰς τόδ᾽ εἷσας
			αὔ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				713
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.75
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔχη</span>
			, <i>boasting, self-confidence,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.62
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.66
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπιθόμβροτον αὔ. δόξας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.92
				</span></i>
			: in pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποῦ τὰ πρόσθεν
			αὐ.</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ax.</u>
				365a
			</span></i>.</div>
